    "gate.title": "Before You Begin",
    "gate.subtitle": "Please read the following legal and ethical boundaries and precautions first.",
    "gate.legal.title": "Legal & Ethical Boundaries",
    "gate.legal.body": "<p>All discussions, sharing, handouts, multimedia content, or any information provided by the organiser, facilitators, or other participants during this event (\"Death Over Dinner\") are for personal experience-sharing and educational purposes only. Such content does not constitute, and cannot replace, professional medical diagnosis, psychological counselling, clinical treatment, financial planning, or legal advice (including, without limitation, formal legal consultation on wills, advance directives, or enduring powers of attorney). Participants with questions in any of these areas should seek assistance from the relevant registered professionals in Hong Kong on their own.</p><p>Participants acknowledge and understand that the life-and-death topics explored in this event may involve emotional, heavy, or sensitive content, and may give rise to emotional distress or psychological discomfort. Participants confirm that their own mental and psychological state is suitable for taking part in this event. During the event, participants retain full autonomy to decline to answer any particular question, to step away temporarily, or to withdraw from the event at any time. To the fullest extent permitted under Hong Kong law, the organiser accepts no responsibility for any psychological or emotional distress not caused by the organiser's negligence.</p><p>Participants must proactively and accurately declare any food allergies, dietary restrictions, or special dietary needs at the time of registration. The organiser will make reasonable efforts to coordinate with third-party catering suppliers, but participants understand and agree that all meals are prepared and provided by third-party restaurants/suppliers. To the fullest extent permitted under Hong Kong law, the organiser accepts no legal liability for any food-related incident, illness, or allergic reaction arising from a third-party supplier's fault, or from a participant's failure to accurately declare an allergen.</p><p>Given the nature of the topics covered, any participant under the age of 18 must be accompanied throughout the event by at least one parent or legal guardian. That parent or legal guardian represents the minor in reading, understanding, and agreeing to all terms of this statement, and agrees to bear full guardianship responsibility for that minor's conduct and emotional state during the event.</p><p>To create a safe and trusted environment for sharing, no audio recording, video recording, or unauthorised photography of any kind is permitted during the event without the explicit consent of both the organiser and the individual concerned. Participants undertake and agree not to disclose, disseminate, or upload to any social media or public platform the personal stories, names, or identifying details shared by other participants during the event. The organiser will handle all participants' personal data in accordance with the Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (Cap. 486) of the Laws of Hong Kong.</p><p>Under the Control of Exemption Clauses Ordinance (Cap. 71) of the Laws of Hong Kong, nothing in this statement excludes or restricts liability for death or personal injury caused by the organiser's negligence. To the fullest other extent permitted by law, the organiser (including its staff and volunteers) accepts no legal or compensatory liability for any loss, damage, or accident to personal property caused by force majeure, third-party acts, or a participant's own negligence. This statement is governed by, and construed in accordance with, the laws of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.</p>",
    "gate.precaution.title": "Important: If You're Currently Experiencing Any of the Following",
    "gate.precaution.body": "If you, or someone you'd like to invite, has recently experienced a sudden death, severe grief, an acute family crisis, or intense emotional distress, we recommend seeking professional support first, and considering a Death Over Dinner once things have settled. This is not an emergency support service and cannot replace professional counselling or medical help.",
    "gate.precaution.urgency": "If you believe this is urgent, or there's any concern for someone's safety, please call one of the hotlines below right away, or go to your nearest hospital emergency department:",
    "gate.precaution.reference": "This guidance follows the general intervention principle used by the Hong Kong Hospital Authority and local bereavement-support organisations: during an acute crisis, connecting to professional support should come before an emotionally demanding family conversation.",
    "gate.crisis.line1": "Hospital Authority 24-hour Mental Health Support Hotline: 18111",
    "gate.crisis.line2": "The Samaritan Befrienders Hong Kong 24-hour hotline: 2389 2222",
    "gate.crisis.line3": "Caritas Family Crisis Support Centre hotline: 18288",
    "gate.ack.label": "I have read and understood the above, and confirm none of the urgent situations described apply right now.",
    "gate.ack.error": "Please confirm you've read and understood the above before starting the questionnaire.",
    "gate.start": "I'm ready, start the questionnaire",

