    "wizard.instructions.title": "How to Answer",
    "wizard.instructions.body": "Across the five themes below, you can skip any theme entirely, and choose more than one card within a theme — there's no theme you must answer, and no minimum number of cards.",

    "theme.reflectionKicker": "Sit with this:",
    "theme.subtitle": "Choose any cards from this theme that fit — or none at all. You've picked {picked} so far (aim for 3 to 5 across the whole dinner).",
    "theme.cardsMax": "Five is the most you can pick — leave room for the conversation itself.",

    "step1.title": "What do you want this dinner to say?",
    "step1.subtitle": "Pick the one closest to how you feel right now.",
    "step1.error": "Please choose one reason so we can understand you better.",
    "intent.acp": "I want to talk with my parents/elders about end-of-life care wishes",
    "intent.loss": "My family recently went through serious illness or loss",
    "intent.repair": "I want to repair or deepen my relationship with a partner or child",
    "intent.legacy": "I simply want to pass down stories and speak from the heart",
    "intent.selfPlan": "I want to sort out my own end-of-life wishes and share them",
    "intent.explore": "No clear purpose yet, just want to try this kind of conversation",
    "step1.crisisNote": "If this involves an urgent crisis, our team will speak with you first to make sure you have enough support.",
    "step1.reflectionPrompt": "What made you decide to come here right now? What was the last straw that brought you to this point?",
    "step1.reflectionLabel": "Your own thoughts (just for you)",
    "step1.reflectionPlaceholder": "There's no right answer — write down whatever comes to mind first…",
    "step1.reflectionNote": "This won't appear in the invitation, and isn't recorded or sent anywhere — it's just for your own reflection.",

    "theme.fate.title": "Fate, Self & Time",
    "theme.fate.reflection": "If you had to write a \"user manual\" for yourself, so the people around you knew how to be with you — what would it say?",
    "card.f1": "At what age did you stop handing the responsibility for your fate to your parents?",
    "card.f2": "If you could rename yourself, what would you choose?",
    "card.f3": "Has your childhood dream come true?",
    "card.f4": "If you had only a year left, would you keep doing what you're doing now?",
    "card.f5": "Looking back from five years from now, are you afraid you'll have regrets?",

    "theme.love.title": "Love & the Words Unsaid",
    "theme.love.reflection": "Watching your partner (or the person closest to you) fast asleep — what runs through your mind?",
    "card.lv1": "How many hands have you held that truly moved you?",
    "card.lv2": "Is there something you've always wanted to thank someone for, or apologise for, but never said?",
    "card.lv3": "Is there something you've wanted to say to someone who was dying, but never did?",
    "card.lv4": "Whose life has the \"ripple\" of yours touched?",
    "card.lv5": "If you could leave one message for the person who matters most, what would it say?",

    "theme.legacy.title": "Meaning, Legacy & Memory",
    "theme.legacy.reflection": "\"True death is when no one in the world remembers you anymore.\" What do you make of that?",
    "card.lg1": "Which side of you do you most want your family to remember?",
    "card.lg2": "If you could leave behind only one object for the next generation, what would it be?",
    "card.lg3": "Write one closing line for the autobiography of your life.",
    "card.lg4": "If you had to write your own epitaph, what would it say?",
    "card.lg5": "What does \"immortality\" mean to you?",
    "card.lg6": "What's the decision in your life you're proudest of?",

    "theme.fear.title": "Fear, Awakening & Loss",
    "theme.fear.reflection": "A thought experiment: one night, a demon whispers that this exact life of yours will repeat itself, identically, an infinite number of times — every joy and every pain, in the same order, forever. Would you curse the demon, or would you answer: \"You are a god, and I have never heard anything more divine\"? If the thought is unbearable, the reason may be simple: some part of you doesn't think this life, as it is, is good enough yet.",
    "card.fr1": "What's your deepest fear about death?",
    "card.fr2": "Have you ever had an experience that felt like a \"wake-up call\"?",
    "card.fr3": "Do you remember the first time someone close to you died?",
    "card.fr4": "Is there a phrase you repeat to yourself when you're afraid?",
    "card.fr5": "Have you ever had a near-death experience? Does it feel the same looking back now?",

    "theme.medical.title": "Medical Wishes & Dignity",
    "theme.medical.reflection": "This theme touches on terminal care, a cancer diagnosis, brain death, organ donation, life-prolonging treatment, dying with dignity, euthanasia, and advance directives — there's no need to have an answer yet. Just notice: which of these words makes you want to look away, and which one have you actually been meaning to bring up with your family?",
    "step5.acpBadge": "Wording pending clinical/social-work review",
    "card.md1": "If one day you're not able to communicate, who do you want making decisions for you?",
    "card.md2": "What does \"dignity\" mean to you in the final stage of life?",
    "card.md3": "Where, and with whom, would you want to spend your final days?",
    "card.md4": "At the very end, what words or music would you want to hear?",
    "card.md5": "Do you want to know how you're going to die?",

    "step6.error": "Please choose 3 to 5 conversation cards in total, across all five themes.",

